WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:05.670
How can you make sure you're getting enough
speaking practice outside the classroom?

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.060
This can be a real challenge for many English
learners.

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:13.000
Let’s take a look at a few ways you can
start practising your speaking.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:20.240
Building your confidence is essential to improving
your speaking.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:25.250
The easiest place to start is with everyday
situations.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:30.140
If you are visiting an English-speaking country,
try following a routine like going to the

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:33.730
same coffee shop every morning to practise
there.

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:37.960
If you feel like a challenge, you could go
to the tourist information centre for directions

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.100
or ideas on what to do.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:46.000
At home, you could focus on a new phrase or
idiom you’ve heard or read, and practise

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.440
using it.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.239
Try repeating it to yourself first.

00:00:50.239 --> 00:00:55.390
I know this sounds ridiculous, but when learning
a new language, we sometimes have to do extreme

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:56.600
things to help us.

00:00:57.409 --> 00:01:01.400
Once you’re ready, you can have a go with
your classmates or friends.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:09.260
Speaking of friends… always remember, you’re not alone!

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:14.000
Chances are there'll be others in your class
who may want to practise their speaking.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:18.600
Set up a regular time with a friend or a group
of friends to talk in English.

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:23.090
If you're a keen cook, you could even host
an evening where you invite a few friends

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:25.500
to come over for dinner and talk in English.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.320
Or maybe you're a keen reader.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.200
Why not start a book group to discuss your
favourite books in English?

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.000
Are you worried that you’re not pronouncing
words properly and this is keeping you from

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.720
practising your spoken English?

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:45.170
Most dictionary websites and apps will have
an audio of the word so you can check the

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:46.270
pronunciation.

00:01:46.270 --> 00:01:50.840
Depending on the app or website you're using,
the accent will be a little bit different.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:56.110
If you are looking for a specific accent,
make sure to include it in your search.

00:01:56.110 --> 00:02:00.710
Practising pronunciation will build your confidence,
which will in turn improve your fluency.

